{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:dependence-free-batch-h1-reviewer-fable-36","reviews":[{"case_id":"case:cc45f160070a5cdcd6b9","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope","bounded_statement":null,"root_cause":null,"issue_class":null,"evidence_atoms":[{"description":"The workflow collapses each digester's eight weekly rows to a single paired change (mean of amended weeks minus mean of baseline weeks) before any test is computed, so each independent unit (digester_id) contributes exactly one analysed value.","observed_value":"one record per digester with change = amended_mean - baseline_mean","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":42,"end_line":43,"quoted_text":"def collapse_to_digesters(log):\n    \"\"\"Reduce the repeated weekly rows to one analysed record per digester.\"\"\""},{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":51,"end_line":60,"quoted_text":"baseline_mean = float(baseline.mean())\n        amended_mean = float(amended.mean())\n        records.append(\n            {\n                \"unit\": unit,\n                \"n_baseline\": int(baseline.size),\n                \"n_amended\": int(amended.size),\n                \"baseline_mean\": baseline_mean,\n                \"amended_mean\": amended_mean,\n                \"change\": amended_mean - baseline_mean,"}]},{"description":"The statistical test is applied only to the 12 per-digester changes, not to the 96 weekly rows: the changes array is built from the collapsed records (one per digester) and passed to scipy.stats.wilcoxon.","observed_value":"stats.wilcoxon called on 12 per-digester changes","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":142,"end_line":145,"quoted_text":"log, n_rows = read_weekly_log(INPUT_PATH)\n    records = collapse_to_digesters(log)\n    changes = np.array([record[\"change\"] for record in records], dtype=float)\n    test = stats.wilcoxon(changes, alternative=\"two-sided\")"}]},{"description":"The reported selected result is internally consistent with n = 12 digesters as the unit of analysis, and the exact two-sided signed-rank p-value for 12 all-positive changes with W = 0 is 2/4096 = 0.000488, exactly matching the report. Independent recomputation of all per-digester means and changes from data/input.csv reproduces the report's table (e.g., D01: 58.90 baseline, 61.25 amended, +2.35), the mean change of +2.500 pp, and the range +1.55 to +3.25.","observed_value":"n = 12, W = 0.0, p = 2/4096 = 0.000488; recomputed table matches report exactly","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":45,"end_line":45,"quoted_text":"[selected-result] Two-sided Wilcoxon signed-rank test on one paired change per digester (n = 12 digesters, 96 weekly readings collapsed): W = 0.0, p = 0.000488; biogas methane content rose in all 12 digesters, mean change +2.500 percentage points (median +2.500, range +1.55 to +3.25)."},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":25,"end_line":25,"quoted_text":"| D01 | 4/4 | 58.90 | 61.25 | +2.35 |"}]},{"description":"The report's stated unit-of-analysis handling matches the data description's requirement: the description names digester_id as the independent unit column and instructs collapsing to one value or one paired change per digester, which is exactly what the workflow does.","observed_value":"declared handling matches prescribed handling","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":15,"end_line":16,"quoted_text":"One row is: one weekly biogas methane reading taken from one digester during one phase of the trial\nIndependent unit column: digester_id"},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":40,"end_line":43,"quoted_text":"The 12 per-digester changes were tested against a null median of zero with a\ntwo-sided Wilcoxon signed-rank test evaluated on its exact null distribution;\nthere are no zero changes and no ties among the absolute changes. The 96\nweekly readings were never entered as 96 independent observations."}]},{"description":"The exact-distribution claim is verified: the 12 recomputed absolute changes (2.35, 1.80, 3.05, 1.55, 2.55, 2.85, 2.05, 3.25, 2.70, 2.20, 3.20, 2.45) are all nonzero and all distinct, so scipy's exact Wilcoxon null distribution applies with no tie or zero corrections.","observed_value":"12 distinct nonzero absolute changes; exact method valid","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":25,"end_line":36,"quoted_text":"| D01 | 4/4 | 58.90 | 61.25 | +2.35 |\n| D02 | 4/4 | 60.15 | 61.95 | +1.80 |\n| D03 | 4/4 | 57.45 | 60.50 | +3.05 |\n| D04 | 4/4 | 61.20 | 62.75 | +1.55 |\n| D05 | 4/4 | 59.60 | 62.15 | +2.55 |\n| D06 | 4/4 | 58.25 | 61.10 | +2.85 |\n| D07 | 4/4 | 60.75 | 62.80 | +2.05 |\n| D08 | 4/4 | 57.90 | 61.15 | +3.25 |\n| D09 | 4/4 | 59.05 | 61.75 | +2.70 |\n| D10 | 4/4 | 60.40 | 62.60 | +2.20 |\n| D11 | 4/4 | 58.55 | 61.75 | +3.20 |\n| D12 | 4/4 | 59.95 | 62.40 | +2.45 |"}]}],"counterevidence_atoms":[{"description":"The raw data do contain repeated entries of each independent unit — every digester_id appears on eight rows (96 rows total for 12 digesters) — so the precondition for the issue class exists in the input; the question is whether those repeated rows reach a row-independent procedure. They do not: the only place row-level values are used is inside the per-digester phase means.","observed_value":"8 rows per digester_id in data/input.csv; used only for within-digester phase means","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":10,"end_line":13,"quoted_text":"The file is stored in long form, one reading per line, so each digester appears\non eight separate lines. Those eight lines are repeated measurements of the same\nvessel and track its individual inoculum, headspace and loading history; they\nare not eight independent pieces of evidence about the supplement."},{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":2,"end_line":9,"quoted_text":"D01,1,baseline,58.4\nD01,2,baseline,59.3\nD01,3,baseline,58.7\nD01,4,baseline,59.2\nD01,5,amended,60.8\nD01,6,amended,61.4\nD01,7,amended,61.1\nD01,8,amended,61.7"}]},{"description":"The report mentions the 96-row count in the selected result, which could superficially suggest row-level analysis; however, the phrasing itself states the readings were collapsed, and the code confirms n_rows is used only as a descriptive count in the report text, never as a sample size in any statistical computation.","observed_value":"n_rows used only in report prose formatting","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":66,"end_line":66,"quoted_text":"def build_report(records, n_rows, changes, test):"},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":5,"end_line":6,"quoted_text":"The file `data/input.csv` is the weekly monitoring log of a pilot digester\ntrial: 96 rows, one row per digester-week gas reading. Twelve independently"}]}],"falsification_attempt":"I tried to demonstrate the issue by tracing every path from row-level data to the test statistic and by recomputing all reported quantities. (1) Code trace: read_weekly_log groups rows by digester_id and phase; collapse_to_digesters averages within digester-phase and emits exactly one change per digester; main passes only that 12-element changes array to stats.wilcoxon. No week-level value reaches the test except through a within-digester mean, and no digester contributes more than one analysed value. (2) Numeric check for a disguised row-level test: I recomputed all 12 per-digester baseline and amended means and changes from data/input.csv and they match the report's table exactly; the mean change is exactly +2.500 and the range +1.55 to +3.25 as reported. With all 12 changes positive and no ties among distinct absolute changes, the exact two-sided Wilcoxon p-value is 2/2^12 = 0.00048828, matching the reported p = 0.000488 and W = 0.0. A test run on the 96 rows would not produce these values (a signed-rank test needs paired values; a 96-row pairing by week is not what the code constructs, and the reported n and p are uniquely consistent with n = 12). (3) I checked whether the reported n or degrees of freedom were inflated anywhere: n is reported as 12 throughout, and the 96-row figure appears only descriptively with the explicit statement that the readings 'were never entered as 96 independent observations.' The falsification attempt failed on all fronts, so the issue class is not demonstrated.","cross_case_evidence_used":false,"unresolved_material_questions":[],"self_reported_confidence":"high"}]}